From 653a199853923705005ef247afa55b59c143fec6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuk3s <44327449+nuk3s@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:10:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kv-offload): reserve the disk tier file at start

Upstream base: the patch applies to local-inference-lab/vllm at
19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 after the 702 patches of
spark-ds41f-1120 (candidate-62, 0001 to 0829) and patches 9030 to 9034
of this series.

Rationale: DiskBackend.init made the tier file with ftruncate, which
creates a sparse file. On a disk that was filling up, the tier therefore
started, and the first write past the free space failed later, in the
middle of serving. This patch reserves the whole file with
posix_fallocate when preallocate is set, which the new
kv_connector_extra_config key disk_preallocate controls (true by default
in the connector and the worker). When the space is not there, init
closes and removes the file and raises OSError with the errno and the
message "cannot reserve N GiB for <path>: <reason>; free space on that
filesystem or lower disk_capacity_bytes" before any IO thread starts, so
the engine start fails at once.

Quality implications: the patch does not change outputs. ext4 and xfs
allocate unwritten extents, so reads return zeros and no data is
written. On a filesystem without fallocate support, glibc falls back to
writing zeros, which writes the whole file at start.

Tests: tests/v1/simple_kv_offload/test_ds41_tier_prealloc.py checks that
a preallocated file has every slot allocated and that the sparse option
allocates nothing. It also checks that an ENOSPC from posix_fallocate
fails init with that errno and the message, leaves no file behind, and
starts no thread. On the CPU path, with VLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu, the
offload suite passed 149 tests, with 2 CUDA-only modules skipped. On DGX
Spark hardware the patch ran only as part of the whole series.

Upstream status: the patch is proposed to spark-ds41f in
experiments/2026-11-22-kv-disk-tier and has not been submitted to
local-inference-lab/vllm.
